{
	"name": "Lamentations",
	"type": "maneuver",
	"img": "icons/magic/symbols/runes-etched-steel-blade.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Calling out a lament to the dead, you work to set them to rest with invocations of the afterlife and lamentations of the loss they left in the world. As an action on your turn, you begin chanting a lamentation which continues until the end of your next turn. Any undead creature within 30ft of you as you chant must make a Charisma save or be [[/condition id=confused]] until the end of your next turn.</p><p>Undead with an Intelligence score of 12 or higher may attempt to make a Charisma save at the start of their turn to break free from the lamentations.</p>",
